mConvexHullFacesAndDuals -- Faces and their duals of a convex hull.
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        mConvexHullFacesAndDuals(L)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note Vector:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Vector,s
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note toFile: toFile, => ..., default value null, Store result in a
        file.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Returns a list of

- a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, A with the vertices of the convex hull
of L in its rows

- a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, Adual with the vertices of the dual in
its rows

- a list of lists with the faces of the convex hull sorted by increasing
dimension.



Each face is a list with two elements. The first is a list of the vertices of
the face, the second a list of the vertices of the dual face.

The vertices of the faces are represented by the indices of the rows of A.

This requires that the convex hull of L contains 0 in its interior.

This uses the Convex functions convHull and faces.



